  --no-reboot: oneof<nothing, bool> # By default, when Amazon EC2 creates the new AMI, it reboots the instance so that it can take snapshots of the attached volumes while data is at rest, in order to ensure a consistent state. You can set the NoReboot parameter to true in the API request, or use the --no-reboot option in the CLI to prevent Amazon EC2 from shutting down and rebooting the instance. If you choose to bypass the shutdown and reboot process by setting the NoReboot parameter to true in the API request, or by using the --no-reboot option in the CLI, we can't guarantee the file system integrity of the created image. Default: false (follow standard reboot process)
